# One byte sequence per file, on every machine.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` system-wide, so without this the
# same commit checks out as CRLF here and LF on a Linux clone. The feature map
# is read by tooling that parses these files as they sit on disk, so the bytes
# should not depend on who cloned it.

* text=auto eol=lf
